<section id="walkthrough" class="student-section" aria-labelledby="walkthrough-title">
    <div class="student-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">CONNECT THE DIAGRAM TO THE CODE</p>
        <h2 id="walkthrough-title">Walk through the application step by step</h2>
    </div>
    <ol class="run-steps">
        <li><div class="step-content"><h3>Create the remote session · arrows 1–7</h3>
            <p>The student clicks <strong>New session</strong>. Blazor sends the click over its SignalR connection, and the <code>CreateAsync</code> handler in <code>Home.razor</code> runs <strong>on the server</strong>. It calls <code>SessionHub.CreateSessionAsync</code>, which calls <code>client.Beta.Sessions.Create</code> with the configured agent ID, environment ID, and a 50¢ list-cost budget. The SDK returns the created session and its ID.</p>
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.HomeCreate" />
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.HubCreate" />
        </div></li>
        <li><div class="step-content"><h3>Prepare observation · arrows 8–12</h3>
            <p>The hub calls <code>AttachAsync(id)</code>. It opens the event stream <strong>before</strong> reading <code>Events.List(id)</code>, so live delivery is buffered while history is paged in. The hub keeps events in a <code>SessionFeed</code> in memory and deduplicates records with IDs. This event buffer is not a durable database.</p>
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.OpenStreamThenHistory" />
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.FeedEmit" />
        </div></li>
        <li><div class="step-content"><h3>Connect the page to the feed · arrows 13–16</h3>
            <p>After preparing the host reader, the hub returns the session ID. <code>Home.razor</code> then subscribes to the feed: it receives the buffered events and registers <code>OnEvent</code> for new ones. There is no browser <code>EventSource</code> and no <code>/api</code> endpoint: the component lives on the server, and Blazor sends each UI change to the browser as a render diff over SignalR. That SignalR connection is separate from the provider stream opened in step 2.</p>
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.AttachOrReport" />
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.ConnectSubscribe" />
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.FeedSubscribe" />
        </div></li>
        <li><div class="step-content"><h3>Send a prompt · arrows 17–21</h3>
            <p>The student enters a prompt and clicks <strong>Send message</strong>. The form's submit handler runs on the server, validates the text, and calls <code>SendMessageAsync</code>. The hub ensures a reader exists with <code>AttachAsync(id)</code> and sends a <code>user.message</code> through <code>Events.Send</code>. The API key remains on the host.</p>
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.HomeSend" />
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.HubSend" />
        </div></li>
        <li><div class="step-content"><h3>Observe the response · arrows 22–25</h3>
            <p>The remote session emits agent and lifecycle events. The SDK delivers them to the hub's background task, which emits them into the feed. Each subscribed component marshals the event onto its renderer, updates the activity feed and session state, and Blazor pushes the change to the browser. An idle event's stop reason may be <code>end_turn</code>, <code>requires_action</code>, or <code>budget_reached</code>; these represent different outcomes.</p>
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.LiveLoop" />
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.OnEvent" />
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.RenderText" />
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.ReadIdle" />
        </div></li>
        <li><div class="step-content"><h3>Keep the session ID and reconnect</h3>
            <p>A completed turn does not create a new conversation or automatically archive the session. On returning from this page in the same tab, the lab restores the last session ID. Click <strong>Connect</strong> to subscribe the page again. The hub reuses its reader if one remains; otherwise, it opens the provider stream and loads history again.</p>
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.RememberSession" />
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.RestoreSession" />
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.ConnectButton" />
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.ReuseReader" />
        </div></li>
    </ol>
</section>
<section class="student-section" aria-labelledby="optional-title">
    <div class="student-heading"><p class="eyebrow">OPTIONAL BRANCHES</p><h2 id="optional-title">When the normal turn needs a host decision</h2></div>
    <div class="architecture-branches with-code">
        <article class="learning-card"><h3>Pending tool action</h3>
            <p>With a suitably configured agent, inspect the event ID and input. The chosen button runs <code>ActionAsync</code> on the server. The hub sends <code>user.tool_confirmation</code> for Allow/Deny, or <code>user.custom_tool_result</code> for a supplied result. These are separate event types. Follow subsequent events to see what happens next.</p>
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.ChooseAction" />
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.ConfirmTool" />
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.CustomResult" />
        </article>
        <article class="learning-card"><h3>Interrupt and inspect</h3>
            <p><strong>Interrupt work</strong> calls <code>InterruptAsync</code>, which sends <code>user.interrupt</code>. Its completion is not proof the remote work stopped. <strong>Inspect session</strong> calls <code>Sessions.Retrieve</code> through the hub. Confirm idle or terminated state; navigating between pages only disconnects the page's view.</p>
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.Interrupt" />
            <CodeExample Snippet="Snippets.Retrieve" />
        </article>
    </div>
    <p class="learning-outcome"><strong>Explain it back:</strong> which two connections carry events (provider stream and Blazor's SignalR circuit), why must the provider stream open before history is read, and which component decides how to respond to a pending action?</p>
</section>
